  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "If $\\text{Var}[X]=3.6,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{10}{3}X].$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{10}{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{10}{3}X] & ={(\\frac{10}{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{9}\\cdot 3.6 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
